      "text": "To find \\(ab + ac + bc\\) for the roots \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\) of the polynomial \\(3x^3 - 3x^2 + 11x - 8 = 0\\), we can use Vieta's formulas. Vieta's formulas relate the coefficients of a polynomial to sums and products of its roots.\n\nFor a cubic polynomial of the form \\(Ax^3 + Bx^2 + Cx + D = 0\\) with roots \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\), Vieta's formulas tell us:\n\\[\na + b + c = -\\frac{B}{A}\n\\]\n\\[\nab + ac + bc = \\frac{C}{A}\n\\]\n\\[\nabc = -\\frac{D}{A}\n\\]\n\nIn our polynomial \\(3x^3 - 3x^2 + 11x - 8 = 0\\), the coefficients are:\n\\[\nA = 3, \\quad B = -3, \\quad C = 11, \\quad D = -8\n\\]\n\nUsing Vieta's formulas, we can find \\(ab + ac + bc\\):\n\\[\nab + ac + bc = \\frac{C}{A} = \\frac{11}{3}\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(ab + ac + bc\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{11}{3}}\n\\]",
